# Userscript versioning

Applies to every `*.user.js` in this repo.

## On every code change

1. **Bump** the `// @version` header in the same change set (do not leave stale versions).
2. Use **semver** (`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`):
   - **PATCH** — fix, polish, copy, logging, small internal refactor with same behavior
   - **MINOR** — new toggle/feature, renamed script/UX change users notice, new `@match` / grants
   - **MAJOR** — breaking rename of storage keys, removed features, incompatible defaults (only when intentional)
3. If several scripts change in one commit, bump **each** touched script’s `@version`.
4. Keep README “current version” (if present) in sync with `@version`.

## Commits

- Put the new version in the **commit subject** (conventional commits), e.g.:
  - `fix(admin-view): hide archived after AJAX reload (v1.7.1)`
  - `feat(admin-view): move toggles to Tampermonkey menu (v2.0.0)`
- One logical change → one version bump that matches that change.
- **Do not** create git tags (`v1.2.3`) unless the user explicitly asks.

## Do not

- Ship userscript edits without a `@version` bump
- Reuse the previous version for a new behavior change
- Add version tags or GitHub Releases by default
